  "verdict": "At the published image positions, 8/11 tracers reproduce the observed residual sign.  Depth tracers (kappa-as-depth, psi background-subtracted bowl depth) and shallowness tracers (flux, |mu|, 1/kappa) are evaluated in their respective sign conventions; the agreement across conventions reflects the single underlying ordering: SX sits at the smallest cluster-centric radius in the densest (near-critical, rescaled kappa = 0.968) environment.  The map/table kappa ratio is uniform at 1.864 (expected 1/beta = 1.873), confirming the documented D_ls/D_s = 1 archive normalisation and mutually validating the map, the Kelly+2023 table, and the image positions.  The FFT Poisson reconstruction ran on the beta-rescaled kappa map.  These point tracers establish an environment ordering only.  Step 56 shows that the corresponding path integral is the GR Fermat/Shapiro contribution already included in the lens model; treating it as an extra static conformal delay would double-count the potential.",
  "caveats": [
    "The archived GLAFIC v3 maps are scaled to D_ls/D_s = 1 (z_s -> infinity; HLSP readme).  At the published image positions the map/table kappa ratio is uniform (mean=1.864, std=0.019, expected 1/beta(1.489) = 1.873); multiplying sampled values by beta = 0.5339 converts them to the SN Refsdal source plane and reproduces the Kelly+2023 Table 15 entries to ~1-3%.",
    "The psi background (psi_bg) is approximated by the map edge/mean/max, which is uncertain because the cluster potential has not decayed to the cosmological background within the ~2.5-arcmin map extent.",
    "The endpoint clock-ratio evaluation (Gamma = 1 + alpha*|Phi_i|/c^2 applied at image positions) is not an additional propagation observable.  The associated path integral is the GR Fermat/Shapiro contribution (Step 56), so reusing it after GR subtraction would be double counting.  The log-magnification proxy remains a phenomenological ansatz requiring an action-derived non-conformal or backreaction transfer kernel.",
    "Image positions are the published J2000 coordinates (refsdal_glafic_v3_lensing_params.json), verified against the archived maps via the uniform beta-rescaled kappa agreement."
